  "notes": "{羨|うらや}む means to envy or feel jealous of what others have.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を particle: Xを{羨|うらや}む (to envy X)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {人|ひと}を{羨|うらや}む: to envy someone\n- {才能|さいのう}を{羨|うらや}む: to envy talent\n- {成功|せいこう}を{羨|うらや}む: to envy success\n- {羨|うらや}んでも{仕方|しかた}がない: it's no use being envious\n\nRELATED FORMS:\n- {羨|うらや}ましい: envious, enviable (i-adjective)\n- {羨望|せんぼう}: envy, admiration (literary noun)\n\nNUANCE:\n{羨|うらや}む and {羨|うらや}ましい express wanting what others have without hostility. For stronger jealousy with resentment, use {嫉妬|しっと}する or {妬|ねた}む.\n\nCONTRAST:\n- {羨|うらや}む: to envy (neutral/positive)\n- {妬|ねた}む: to be jealous (with resentment)\n- {嫉妬|しっと}する: to be jealous (strong emotion)",
